The convention is verified: cosine 1.0 and norm ratio 1.0 at all three layers. Now the actual test. I project the `(` positions (the last token of all 319 D2 texts) onto each refit detector and compare them with the PDF classes, giving mean, 5th/95th percentile and the share above 0.3. Under my hypothesis, at least one detector, most likely e6m at L15, is clearly positive at `(`.

```python
# Hypothesis: a detector fires at '(' after the def name (gate opens there -> copies the prompt's token after 'name(').
proj_paren = {}
for L in (15,19,23):
    Xp = np.stack([np.asarray(xnorm(np.asarray(H8[i, li[L], L8[i]-1], dtype=np.float32), lnw[L]), dtype=np.float32).ravel() for i in range(len(L8))])
    proj_paren[L] = Xp @ dirs[L]
rows_out = []
for L in (15,19,23):
    pr = np.asarray(XF[L], dtype=np.float32) @ dirs[L]
    d = {'layer': L, 'paren(': proj_paren[L]}
    for c in ['def','start','mid','last','other']:
        d[c] = pr[(PDF.cls==c).values]
    rows_out.append({k: (f'{np.mean(v):.2f} [{np.percentile(v,5):.2f},{np.percentile(v,95):.2f}] >.3:{np.mean(v>.3):.2f}' if k!='layer' else v) for k,v in d.items()})
print(pd.DataFrame(rows_out).to_string(index=False))
```

